# Task: rotate logs with logrotate using an explicit configuration and state file.
# Program: this file.
# Run: execute docs/recipes/server-rotate-logs.program --input config=/etc/logrotate.d/myapp.conf
# Test with fakes: put a fake `logrotate` earlier on PATH that prints its arguments. Expect
#   --state, the state path, then the config path. Make it exit 1 to check the failure line.
# Explain: the program reports only a failure; logrotate writes its own messages.
# Replaces (Bash): logrotate --state "$STATE" "$CONFIG"
# Limit: needs the rights to read the config and write the state file, usually root.
accept config as text with default "/etc/logrotate.conf"
accept state_file as text with default "/var/lib/logrotate/logrotate.status"
run "logrotate" with arguments ["--state", state_file, config] and keep status as code
if code is not 0
  run "printf" with arguments ["logrotate failed for %s (status %s)\n", config, code]
  run "false"
